tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Storer","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10909","person_slug":"tim-storer","vote":"no"}],"name":"Documents - Future Submarine Project; Order for the Production of Documents - Sitting placement","noes":37,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2018-09-17.4.2) introduced by Centre Alliance Senator [Rex Patrick](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/sa/rex_patrick) (SA), which means it failed. One senator - [Brian Burston](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/brian_burston) (NSW) - [crossed the floor](https://www.peo.gov.au/learning/fact-sheets/crossing-the-floor.html), voting \"No\" against the majority of the Pauline Hanson's One Nation Party. ### Motion text > *That—* > *The Senate resolves that until such time as the Senate by resolution is satisfied that the order for the production of documents relating to the submarine project (No. 862) has been complied with, the Minister representing the Minister for Defence Industry shall be prohibited from sitting in the front bench seats reserved for Ministers and be allocated a seat by the President in another seat.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-5420","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2018-09-17/1"}
